# Vendored third-party source under third_party/.
#
# One entry per library, separated by a line holding only "---". An entry has
# these fields, one per line:
#
#   directory: <path below third_party/>
#   module:    <upstream module path>
#   version:   <upstream tag or commit>
#   changed:   <file> <sha256> <commit>[,<commit>...]
#   deleted:   <file>
#
# "changed" names every file that differs from the module at that version,
# including a file that exists only in the vendored copy, with the SHA-256 of
# its vendored content and the commits in this repository that introduced the
# change, oldest first. "deleted" names every upstream file absent from the
# vendored copy. A file with no local change has neither a changed nor a
# deleted line.
#
# Lines starting with "#" and blank lines are ignored. scripts/check-third-party
# downloads each module at the recorded version through the Go module proxy and
# checksum database and compares it file by file with the vendored copy, so an
# unlisted change, a missing file, a listed change that no longer exists, a
# recorded hash that no longer matches the vendored bytes and a symbolic link
# all fail the check.

